<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0001007> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0001005> ;
                                              rdfs:label "thin layer chromatography"@en ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "TLC"@en ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chromatography method where the stationary phase is a thin (0.10 to 0.25 mm) layer of sorbent applied to a firm backing such as glass, aluminium or plastic sheet. An eluent ( single solvent or solvent mixture) is allowed to flow by capillary action through the sorbent starting at a point just below the applied samples. As the eluent front migrates through the sorbent the components of the sample also migrate, but at different rates resulting in separation. [CHMO]"@en ;
                                              <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasDomain> "Chem"@en ;
                                              <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasStudyStage> "Analysis" ;
                                              <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasSubDomain> "Chem-Rxn"@en .


