###  https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/DielectricConstant
<https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/DielectricConstant> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/AnalyticalResult> ,
                                                                       <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/ElectricalProperty> ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "It is defined as the ratio of a capacitor's capacitance with a dielectric material to its capacitance with a vacuum, or the ratio of the material's permittivity to the permittivity of free space. A higher dielectric constant indicates that a material is better at insulating and storing charge, while a lower constant means it is closer to a vacuum's insulating properties."@en ;
                                                       rdfs:label "DielectricConstant"@en ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "" ,
                                                                                                      "Relative permittivity" ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dielectric constant is also known as relative permittivity and it is a measure of a measure of a material's ability to store electrical energy in an electric field compared to a vacuum. "@en ,
                                                                                                        "Electrical permittivity"@en ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This property is for a cured polymer. "@en ;
                                                       <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasDomain> "Chem"@en ;
                                                       <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasStudyStage> "Sample" ;
                                                       <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasSubDomain> "Chem-Form"@en .


