                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> " " ;
                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "It sometimes refers to the discrimination shown by a given reactant A when it reacts with two alternative reactants B and C, or in two different ways (e.g. at two different sites) with a reactant B. The term also sometimes refers to the ratio of products obtained from given reactants. This meaning is of importance for catalysts, which can have a wide range of selectivities. Selectivity is quantitatively expressed by ratios of rate constants for the alternative reactions, or by the decadic logarithms of such ratios.[IUPAC]"@en ;
                                                <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasDomain> "Chem"@en ;
                                                <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasStudyStage> " " ;
                                                <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasSubDomain> "Chem-Rxn"@en ;
                                                <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001754> "https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.S05563"@en .


###  https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/Semiconductor
<https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/Semiconductor> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/Material>
                                                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                               owl:onProperty <https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/hasElectronicBandGap> ;
